 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\equiv x(p^{\prime},w^{\prime})$
\end_inset

.
 Note that 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C(A)\subseteq A$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in C(B)\subseteq B$
\end_inset

.
 Now, suppose 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in B$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x\neq x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

.
 We want to show that 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\notin A$
\end_inset

.
 Suppose for contradiction that 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in A$
\end_inset

.
 So, we have 
\begin_inset Formula $\{A,B\}\subseteq\mathcal{B}^{W}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\{x,x^{\prime}\}\subseteq A\cap B$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C(A)$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in C(B)$
\end_inset

