.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\{A,B\}\subseteq\mathcal{B}^{W}$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ \{p,p^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{++}^{2},\ \exists\ \{w,w^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}:A\equiv B(p,w)\ \wedge\ B\equiv B(p^{\prime},w^{\prime})$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C(A)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in C(B)$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $x\equiv x(p,w)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\equiv x(p^{\prime},w^{\prime})$
\end_inset

, respectively.
 Also, 
\begin_inset Formula $\{x,x^{\prime}\}\subseteq A\cap B\implies\left[x\in A\ \wedge\ x\in B\right]\ \wedge\ \left[x^{\prime}\in A\ \wedge\ x^{\prime}\in B\right]$
\end_inset

.
 Finally, since 
\begin_inset Formula $x\notin C(B)$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $x\neq x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

.
 So, we have 
\begin_inset Formula $p^{\prime}\cdot x\leq w^{\prime}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x\neq x^{\prime}$
\end_inset

, which implies that 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{\prime}>w$
\end_inset

 by our assumption.
 However, this contradicts the fact that 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\prime}\in A\equiv B(p,w)$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $(\rightarrow\leftarrow)$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $(\mathcal{B}^{W},C)$
\end_inset

 satisfies WARP .
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof

\bar under
Part B.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
