\end_inset

 be a demand function that is homoenous of degree zero and satisfies Walras'
 Law.
 We prove that WARP is equivalent to the following property: 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \{p,p^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{++}^{2}:p^{\prime}\cdot x(p,1)<1\implies p\cdot x(p^{\prime},1)>1$
