 satisfies WARP, which, by the result of Problem 9(A), Section 3.4.8, is equivalen
t to the following property for deman functions in a competitive environment:
 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \{p,p^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{++}^{2},\ \forall\ \{w,w^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}:\left[p^{\prime}\cdot x(p,w)\leq w^{\prime}\ \wedge\ x(p,w)\neq x(p^{\prime},w^{\prime})\right]\implies p\cdot x(p^{\prime},w^{\prime})>w$
